rule: ELIM-G-3, ELIM-G-19
One copy of iter per static function argument; the static argument's
closure is the key, compared by label, and the atoms are the parameters.
CHECK-DAG: -- specialization of Main.iter(lam{{[0-9]+}}[]; _:Int; _:Int)
CHECK-DAG: Main.iter#1 (%{{[0-9]+}} : w Int) (%{{[0-9]+}} : w Int) : Int =
CHECK-DAG: Main.iter#2 (%{{[0-9]+}} : w Int) (%{{[0-9]+}} : w Int) : Int =
CHECK-DAG: add_Int(1:Int, %{{[0-9]+}})
CHECK-DAG: mul_Int(2:Int, %{{[0-9]+}})
CHECK-DAG: = Main.iter#1(%{{[0-9]+}}, %{{[0-9]+}})
CHECK-DAG: = Main.iter#2(%{{[0-9]+}}, %{{[0-9]+}})
rule: CORE-OPT-1
First-order calls with runtime arguments stay calls; MLIR inlines them.
CHECK-DAG: = Main.iter#2(%{{[0-9]+}}, 1:Int)
